V89 joint row accounting audit

Command: python3 scripts/cu66-v89/audit_joint.py
Observed exit code: 0
Observed stdout: V89_JOINT_ACCOUNTING_AUDIT_PASS rows=64 native_packets=64 summary_groups=16
Observed stderr: (empty)

The independent check verified 33 source pins, the 64 unique rows covering four
sources × four policies × LOW/HIGH × alias/no-alias, and packet SHA-256 and byte
counts against the selected V88 native wire rows. It recomputed min/median/max,
totals and under-10-ms counts for all 16 four-row groups. Same-source paired
comparisons against AB38_control show feedback_overhead5 regressed in 14/16
comparisons (median +582 cycles; total +8,321 cycles), while feedback_overhead15
regressed in 10/16 (median +504 cycles; total -1,004,399 cycles). all_BR88 also
has six regressions despite improving overall. Thus latency benefit depends on
the policy and source. These are modeled schedule comparisons, not hardware
qualification; the separate stored-DAG audit covers schedule structure.
